 "captions": {
  "script": "This isn't snow. It's water turning into stone. Glitch Diary, entry four. Pamukkale, Turkey. The name means \"cotton castle.\" Warm spring water spills down a cliff almost two hundred meters high, loaded with calcium carbonate. As it releases gas, the mineral hardens into white travertine, terrace after terrace. But that's not the strange part. On top sits Hierapolis, an ancient spa city where people bathed two thousand years ago. Last century, hotels were built on the terraces and damaged them. They were torn down. Today you must walk barefoot. And there's something even stranger. Nearby is a shrine the Romans called the Gate to Hell. Its volcanic gas still kills birds that fly too close. Would you walk on a waterfall made of stone? Comment below. Follow for the next entry of my glitch diary. Because this isn't snow...",
